use @piton/belay
from ../Factory import Factory
from ./lib/FactorySkillBase import FactorySkillBase

export skill Factory0010Start extends FactorySkillBase:
    description: Start or resume a project factory, reconciling saved work and surviving sessions.
    useWhen: starting a configured project factory or resuming it after shutdown or interruption
    prompt:
        Discover the actual startup operations and approved configuration.
        Check whether the factory is already running; use the existing instance
        rather than start duplicate services. Starting this skill authorizes
        startup within the established operating policy, not new budgets or
        capabilities. If setup is missing, identify what onboarding must supply.

        Follow @{Factory.restartRecovery}, @{Factory.failedAttempts}, and
        @{Factory.operationRetries}. Inspect preserved orders, plans, step
        attempts, briefs, results, worktrees, operation requests, and harness
        session references before issuing new execution requests.

        Reconcile each affected attempt with the harness and artifact evidence.
        Reconnect to surviving sessions and let them continue. Do not launch
        replacements for work still running or blindly repeat completed work.
        A disconnected client is not proof that the underlying session ended.
        Keep uncertain liveness explicit and investigate through supported
        harness operations before claiming a safe replacement.

        Report recovered implementation results through the normal higher-level
        completion assessment. Preserve superseded outputs for possible reuse;
        they do not automatically satisfy the revised plan. Respect changed
        prerequisite versions and pending reconciliation.

        Use configured limited retries for temporary execution failures and
        reuse the original operation request identifier when its outcome is
        uncertain. Exhausted retries and substantive work problems enter the
        agent escalation path. Obtain engineer input when resolution looks
        unlikely; do not reset attempt history to create endless retries.
        Update state through factory operations, not direct database repair.
        After reconciliation, start or resume dispatch through the actual
        factory controls within approved limits. Verify service health and
        dispatch state. Do not claim readiness from process existence alone.

    result:
        Report surviving sessions, recovered results, uncertain attempts,
        retries or escalations, and the evidence that prevents duplicate work.
